{"title":"Euclid's Lemma","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p><b>Euclid's Lemma</b> is a result in <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">number theory</a> attributed to <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclid\" title=\"Euclid\">Euclid</a>. It states that:\n</p><p>A positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8569597fbeeb665b4eed107b72b03ff2a00c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime_number\" title=\"Prime number\">prime number</a> if and only if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb5ee561b6ba4711a0df8172c374a13225ec748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> implies that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/e/49effd714e2e2e48f30508247323a394e94a0212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/f/2ef0207b7e9bfd294ad4c1271944f143dc36a8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\mid b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, for all <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integers</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Proof_of_Euclid.27s_Lemma\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Proof_of_Euclid's_Lemma\">Proof of Euclid's Lemma</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclid%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Proof of Euclid&#39;s Lemma\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/d/f8db4449bcd313c6d4d21d1264949d4a1b80337b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\gcd(p,a)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"18\" /> (otherwise we are done).  By <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Bezout%27s_Lemma\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Bezout&#39;s Lemma\">Bezout's Lemma</a>, there exist integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b6400c6fe3f1ed70e5afd387a9686cdc3fa09531.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/5/ca50d574e04387473595ac6c3fec39f19f1b0fbe.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$px+ay=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"94\" height=\"15\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/0/d500cd7dfa6626a463c2bce8f8ff9bf2363f698c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b(px+ay)=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"115\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/9/299dae068b84a767ce95860ccd85ea945ca5e0cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$pbx+aby=b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/2/21246ca64e21239013fecc6ffdcb9e2802f3a58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\mid p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/b/beb5ee561b6ba4711a0df8172c374a13225ec748.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> (by hypothesis), <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/437d8be83b981c290074eba3bbf05a1521bd865e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\mid pbx + aby =b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"134\" height=\"18\" />, as desired.\n</p><p>On the other hand, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/8/be8569597fbeeb665b4eed107b72b03ff2a00c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is not prime, then it must be composite, i.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa27c3f697ef793580b73e04d313d620441d2481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=ab$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, for integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9bdf3e496517e8f8742f81dd774be1f93cf6e8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> both greater than 1.  Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f294a58cc4762402465aa9b0097757cec749883a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\nmid a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/5/9151a2c8bba716e2eb97f5adce8b5a25dcd23f36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\nmid b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />. \n</p><p>This completes the proof.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclid%27s_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Fundamental_theorem_of_arithmetic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Fundamental theorem of arithmetic\">Fundamental theorem of arithmetic</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Euclid\" title=\"Euclid\">Euclid</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Number_theory\" title=\"Number theory\">Number theory</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018071859\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.012 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visi